{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "דוה", :translit "daveh", :gloss "sickly"} {:he "תזרם כמו דוה", :translit "tizrach kemo daveh", :gloss "you shall flow like a sickly one"} {:he "כל היום דוה", :translit "kol ha-yom daveh", :gloss "all the day sickly"} {:he "ע\"ג", :translit "avodah zarah", :gloss "idolatry"} {:he "מטמאה כנדה", :translit "m'tameh k'niddah", :gloss "impure like a menstruant"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["דוה" "תזרם כמו דוה" "כל היום דוה"]}], :frame {:text "The word דוה (sickly) appears in Leviticus 20:18 for a menstruant and in Lamentations 5:17 for the devastation of Zion described as כל היום דוה. The reading of Lamentations over destruction (Megillah 13b) and the association of idolatry with menstrual impurity (Shabbat 13a) together link the verse's language of impurity to the consequences of idolatrous worship.", :sources ["Leviticus 20:18" "Lamentations 5:17" "Megillah 13b" "Shabbat 13a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מקורה", :translit "m'korah", :gloss "her spring"} {:he "והובשתי את מקורה", :translit "v'hovshti et m'korah", :gloss "and I will dry up her spring"} {:he "מקורה יבש מקורה", :translit "m'korah yaveish m'korah", :gloss "her spring dry her spring"} {:he "ערירים יהיו", :translit "aririm yihyu", :gloss "they shall be barren"} {:he "ולא תוליד", :translit "v'lo t'lid", :gloss "and you shall not give birth"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["מקורה" "והובשתי את מקורה"]}], :frame {:text "The word מקורה (her flow/spring) appears in Leviticus 20:18 and in Hosea 9:14 — והובשתי את מקורה ('and I will dry up her spring'). The Hosea verse concludes with ערירים יהיו ('they shall be barren'), linking the terminology of bodily flow to the curse of childlessness.", :sources ["Leviticus 20:18" "Hosea 9:14"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הערה", :translit "he'irah", :gloss "he emitted"} {:he "כי את שארו הערה", :translit "ki et she'eiro he'irah", :gloss "for his fleshly emission he emitted"} {:he "אשר הערה למות נפשו", :translit "asher he'irah l'mut nafsho", :gloss "which he emitted for the death of his soul"} {:he "שארו הערה", :translit "she'eiro he'irah", :gloss "his fleshly emission he emitted"} {:he "הערה למות נפשו", :translit "he'irah l'mut nafsho", :gloss "an emission for the death of his soul"} {:he "בעדים והתראה", :translit "b'edim v'hatra'ah", :gloss "with witnesses and warning"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["הערה" "כי את שארו הערה" "אשר הערה למות נפשו"]}], :frame {:text "The word הערה appears in Leviticus 20:18 and in Leviticus 15:32 — כי את שארו הערה — describing a zivah emission. Capital punishment in Jewish law requires testimony by valid witnesses and a prior warning to the transgressor (Sanhedrin 40b). The linkage of the word to למות נפשו ('for the death of a soul') is found in Leviticus 20:27.", :sources ["Leviticus 20:18" "Leviticus 15:32" "Leviticus 20:27" "Sanhedrin 40b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מקור דמיה", :translit "m'kor dameha", :gloss "the flow of her blood"} {:he "דמי ה, שה", :translit "d'mei hei, shin hei", :gloss "bloods of [the letter] hei, shin hei"} {:he "דמים טמאים באשה", :translit "d'mim t'mei'im b'ishah", :gloss "impure bloods in a woman"} {:he "אשת רעהו", :translit "eishet re'ehu", :gloss "another man's wife"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "דמיה", :expansion ["דמי" "ה" "שה"]} {:kind :other, :note "Interpretive reading of מקור דמיה as 'impure bloods in a woman' via splitting דמיה into דמי-ה-שה"}], :frame {:text "The phrase מקור דמיה appears in Leviticus 20:18 in the context of the prohibition against relations with a menstruant. The Talmud derives that the prohibition of adultery applies specifically with another man's wife (Sanhedrin 54b). The phrase that God is filled with anger recalls the language of divine wrath (Ezekiel 16:38).", :sources ["Leviticus 20:18" "Sanhedrin 54b" "Ezekiel 16:38"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["דוה" "תזרם כמו דוה" "כל היום דוה"], :by :selah, :located [{